E4EF                             ;  Machine code: the grave
E4EF                             ; =============================================================================
E4EF                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E4EF                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E4EF                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E4EF                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E4EF                             ; contract in the header.
E4EF   20 2F E5     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E4F2   B0 2D                  BCS   exec   
E4F4   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E4F5   0A                     ASL      
E4F6   0A                     ASL      
E4F7   0A                     ASL      
E4F8   85 04                  STA   T0   
